events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Because of the use of Godot Android as a library; In the `lib` module the behavior of enabling / disabling edge-to-edge and / or immersive is applied to all consumers of the library regardless of whether they want it or not. \r\nThis can cause issues if a developer decides to integrate Godot into their project as a sub-piece of a larger UI, and want to handle edge-to-edge on their own.\r\n\r\nBy moving the logic into `app` and `editor`, that behavior is applied only to our projects as we have a specific way we want to use it. The methods are still public if other users of the Android library want to make use of the same capabilities.","created_at":"2025-06-21T15:11:22Z","updated_at":"2025-06-21T15:11:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#discussion_r2160061591","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107742","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2160061591"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742#discussion_r2160061591"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107742"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2160061591/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":77,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2159850784,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":36,"position":36,"subject_type":"line"}]